><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20251113103936+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="959a2428-0b98-4303-94f0-27f0aaed4a6f" date="D:20251113103941+10'00'" name="080faa04-f1c1-4026-b299-1662380a9b6c" icon="Comment" page="7" rect="64.835500,580.465000,88.835500,604.465000" subject="Sticky Note" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>In summary, the following recommendations&#xD;for IMU positions are suggested to&#xD;improve the similarity between IMU relative angles&#xD;and gold standard relative angles:&#xD;(a) For sports and activities where transverse plane&#xD;rotation of the upper torso (thorax) relative to&#xD;the pelvis is of interest: sensors positioned on&#xD;the posterior pelvis and over the sternum,&#xD;(b) For sports and activities where transverse&#xD;plane rotation of the lower torso relative to&#xD;the pelvis is of interest: sensors positioned on&#xD;the posterior pelvis and at T2,&#xD;(c) For sports and activities where measuring&#xD;frontal plane rotation of the upper torso&#xD;(thorax) relative to the pelvis is of interest:&#xD;sensors positioned on the posterior pelvis and&#xD;at T2.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="7" rect="609.449000,512.465000,793.449000,604.465000"
/></text
></annots
><f href="../pdfs/10.1080_17461391.2019.1666167.pdf"
/><ids original="58FA22291389E83B57930C38FF198A4E" modified="F46CA0ABA4CE2C458B48F674F7D1C36F"
/></xfdf
>